- This is the OpenABL 1.2 kit. It boots Boot Loader Spec entries (/loader/entries/*.conf,
  /Image, /dtbs/*.dtb) that pocknix already writes to the boot FAT, NOT the Android /KERNEL.
- Only flash it once those files are present and Pocknix boots with the ROCKNIX ABL.
- Copy the openabl folder from the SD card to the root of Android Internal Storage
- Execute as root the backup_abl.sh script from the Internal Storage to backup your current ABL
- After backup, execute as root the flash_abl.sh script to flash OpenABL
- Reboot your device holding Vol - key to enter fastboot menu
- Select "Change boot mode" option using Vol -/+ key, and hit Power button
- First start: OpenABL asks for the Device model. Set it (or the screen stays black), then Start.
- Going back: restore_backup_abl.sh puts the original bootloader back (abl_a.img / abl_b.img).
